---
import { CORPUS_SECTIONS, CORPUS_UPDATED, SDK_VERSION, MANUAL_VERSION } from '../lib/config';
import corpus from '../../../worker/src/lib/corpus-info.json';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
export const prerender = true;
---
<Base
  title="About Sharp AI"
  description="How Sharp AI indexes FIRST Tech Challenge documentation, what it will and will not answer, and why it carries no advertising."
>
  <section class="wrap ab">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Where the answers come from.</h1>

    <div class="ab__body prose">
      <p class="serif-lede">
        Sharp AI searches FTC documentation and then writes up what it found.
        Retrieved sections appear beside the answer so you can inspect its support.
        It can also offer general engineering reasoning, which is shown separately
        as uncited and unverified. A source link or wording match is not proof
        that a generated claim is correct.
      </p>

      <h2>What is indexed</h2>
      <p>
        {CORPUS_SECTIONS.toLocaleString()} sections across {corpus.sources.length} sources, refreshed {CORPUS_UPDATED}. The big ones are the official
        <a href="https://ftc-docs.firstinspires.org" rel="noopener">FTC Docs</a>,
        <a href="https://docs.revrobotics.com" rel="noopener">REV</a>,
        <a href="https://gm0.org" rel="noopener">Game Manual 0</a>, the FTC SDK
        javadocs and sample OpModes, <a href="https://www.chiefdelphi.com" rel="noopener">Chief
        Delphi</a>, <a href="https://pedropathing.com" rel="noopener">Pedro Pathing</a>,
        Road Runner, <a href="https://www.ctrlaltftc.com" rel="noopener">CTRL ALT FTC</a>
        and <a href="https://docs.ftclib.org" rel="noopener">FTCLib</a>. Everything is split
        by heading section, so a citation lands on the part of the page it came from
        rather than the top of it.
      </p>

      <h2>Three levels of access</h2>
      <p>
        What a source lets us do with its text decides how it gets used, and the
        rule is applied on the server when the prompt is assembled, not in the
        page you are reading.
      </p>
      <p>
        Game Manual 0, the FTC Docs and the SDK reference publish open licences,
        so they are read in full and quoted with a citation.
      </p>
      <p>
        The <em>FIRST</em> Competition Manual and the Pedro Pathing docs are
        summarised but never quoted. You get the substance in Sharp AI’s own
        words plus a link, and their text is never stored on an answer page.
      </p>
      <p>
        REV, Chief Delphi, Road Runner, CTRL ALT FTC and FTCLib publish no
        licence, which means all rights reserved. Only the page title, its place
        in the docs and the URL are stored. Ask about Road Runner tuning and you
        get the page named and linked, rather than a paraphrase of something we
        have no right to reproduce or a guess improvised from a nearby page.
      </p>

      <h2>What is deliberately not indexed</h2>
      <p>
        LearnRoadRunner is excluded: it documents Road Runner 0.5 and would
        produce confidently wrong answers for teams on current versions.
      </p>
      <p>
        The indexed BIOBUZZ Competition Manual ({MANUAL_VERSION}) and FTC SDK {SDK_VERSION} are indexed.
        Official Team Q&amp;A rulings remain authoritative and are linked separately at
        <a href="https://ftc.game" rel="noopener">ftc.game</a>. Check both before relying on a rule interpretation.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/sources">Search and inspect the source notebook ↗</a></p>
      <h2>Source coverage</h2>
      <div class="ab__coverage"><table><thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Sections</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        {corpus.sources.map((source) => <tr><td><a href={source.homepage} rel="noopener">{source.name}</a></td><td>{source.sections}</td><td>{source.mode === 'full' ? 'Cited excerpts' : source.mode === 'summarize' ? 'Summaries' : 'Titles & links'}</td></tr>)}
      </tbody></table></div>
      <h2>Your conversations</h2>
      <p>Conversation history is saved on this browser, with no account or public share page.
        Saved chats retain the grounded answer and its sources. The separate general reasoning section is not saved.
        Export a conversation as Markdown to keep a copy, or remove it from History.</p>

      <h2>Why there are no ads</h2>
      <p>
        Game Manual 0 is published under
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/" rel="license noopener">CC BY-NC 4.0</a>.
        Non-commercial means non-commercial. This site will never carry
        advertising, a paid tier or a sponsorship, for as long as it uses that
        corpus.
      </p>

      <h2>When the index has a gap</h2>
      <p>
        Retrieval scores help decide whether the index covers a question. When
        support is missing, the reply can include separately labeled general
        reasoning. That reasoning is not evidence from the indexed sources and
        is not retained in saved chats. Quota or model failures can return
        documentation sections without a generated answer.
      </p>

      <h2>Verify everything that matters</h2>
      <p>
        Answers are model-written from retrieved text and can be wrong. The
        source section is shown beside every answer so you can check it in one
        glance. For anything rules-related, the official Game Manual is the only
        authority.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .ab { padding: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.5rem) 0 2rem; max-width: 52rem; }
  .ab h1 { margin: 0.8rem 0 1.8rem; max-width: 14ch; }
  .ab__body { max-width: 40rem; }
  .ab__body .serif-lede { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .ab__coverage { overflow-x: auto; }
  .ab__coverage table { width: 100%; font-size: .8rem; border-collapse: collapse; }
  .ab__coverage th, .ab__coverage td { text-align: left; padding: .55rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .ab__body a { color: var(--accent); border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 30%, transparent); }
  .ab__body a:hover { border-bottom-color: var(--accent); }
</style>
